The revenue value stated in the Annual Report 2020 for the year 2020 is NOK 3,539,231 thousand.

### 2. Task outcome (extremely detailed version):
According to the "Consolidated income statement" section of the "LINK Annual Report 2020", the total operating revenue for the period ended 31 December 2020 was NOK 3,539,231 thousand. For the prior year, 2019, the revenue was NOK 2,890,025 thousand.

Additionally, the "Link Mobility Group Holding ASA - Prospectus" provides a "Condensed consolidated statement of income" and a table reconciling "Like-for-Like Revenue to revenue". In the "Condensed consolidated statement of income" (excerpt_1), the "Total operating revenue" for the year ended 31 December 2019 is reported as NOK 2,932,707 thousand, for 2018 as NOK 1,972,009 thousand, and for 2017 as NOK 1,294,002 thousand. The "Revenue" in the reconciliation table (excerpt_2) for the year ended 31 December 2019 is NOK 2,932.7 million (equivalent to NOK 2,932,700 thousand), for 2018 as NOK 1,972.0 million, and for 2017 as NOK 1,294.0 million.

It is important to note a slight difference in the reported 2019 revenue between the "LINK Annual Report 2020" (NOK 2,890,025 thousand) and the "Link Mobility Group Holding ASA - Prospectus" (NOK 2,932,707 thousand or NOK 2,932.7 million). This discrepancy could be due to re-audits, adjustments, or different reporting standards/periods between the annual report and the prospectus.

### 3. Additional context (if relevant):
The revenue figures are presented in Norwegian Krone (NOK) and are in thousands (NOK 1000) in the consolidated income statement of the Annual Report 2020. The prospectus also presents some figures in NOK million. The annual report also details how revenue is generated, primarily from the sale of services enabling mobile phone communication, split into mobile messaging transactions, payment services, licenses, and consulting services. Revenue recognition varies based on the type of service, for instance, mobile messaging revenue is recognized when messages are delivered, and payment services revenue is recognized as income from processed transactions.
